2027 polls, the use of artificial intelligence in the electoral process has prompted questions about integrity and institutional readiness. Can Nigerians trust their democratic processes?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>South Sudan pushes back elections amid violent flare-ups</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d3a0eaba929e8f2ed614595ddc68bfa60e6fbf5967767edc30d557c90996942f</id><updated>2026-11-15T15:44:10Z</updated><published>2026-11-14T20:53:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/south-sudan-pushes-back-elections-amid-violent-flare-ups/a-79949622--9cf2f881ff78.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/south-sudan-pushes-back-elections-amid-violent-flare-ups/a-79949622?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">South Sudan has been independent from Sudan since 2011, and has not yet held national elections. Since then, the country faces cycles of violence after a civil war led to a tenuous peace deal.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Senegal Youth Olympics in Dakar end on high note</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b1fdc9c98e8d841ac9db745611c7fbf9b3636e1f2883efd8f47dfa8a7881fd0c</id><updated>2026-11-15T15:44:10Z</updated><published>2026-11-14T04:25:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/senegal-youth-olympics-in-dakar-end-on-high-note/a-79944820--d8ec73fdda7d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/senegal-youth-olympics-in-dakar-end-on-high-note/a-79944820?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Enthusiastic crowds attended the games in Senegal, with China taking home the most gold medals. It's the first Olympic Games since Russia's war on Ukraine where Russian athletes can compete under their own flag.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Wael Mohya could make German football history at 17</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:20672002626114fba9573e25626b1a4cdc0642454